      {
         "id": "SECTION_game",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Practice Exercise\n\nReading a text may seem sufficient, but practice is essential for true understanding. In the following table, we will practice subtracting two numbers. The top number will always be larger than the bottom one. However, in some cases, in certain columns (units, tens, or hundreds), the digit of the top number may be smaller than the one below. When this happens, you need to regroup: mark the original number in black and write the regrouped value above it.\n\nBefore using the controls (<i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-up upArrowWithFA\" style=\"font-size: 1.5em\" name=\"traineeUp\"></i> <i class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-down downArrowWithFA\" style=\"font-size: 1.5em\" name=\"traineeDown\"></i>) to check your answer, try solving it on your own.\n\nWhen you finish the calculation, you will receive a medal (<i class=\"fa-solid fa-medal\" style=\"color:gold;\"></i>) and can move on to the next problem by clicking the arrow (<i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right\"></i>) below:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"htSequenceGame\" id=\"cmp0\"><table id=\"yupana0\" class=\"tawapukllay\"><tr><th colspan=\"4\">Subtraction of Numbers</th><th colspan=\"2\">Controls</th></tr> </table></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 1</b>: Exercise for Subtracting Two Numbers.</p>",
